- [x] Add
  `src/dwarfspec/automation/base_screen_focus_guard.lua` with injected GUI
  dependencies.
- [x] Capture the base screen with `dfhack.gui.getDFViewscreen(true)`.
- [x] Distinguish successful `present`, successful `none`, and failed
  `unavailable` screen capture.
- [x] Store exact screen identity only in the private comparison token.
- [x] Produce bounded detached screen and focus diagnostics.
- [x] Copy and canonicalize focus strings without retaining or modifying
  DFHack-owned tables.
- [x] Return explicit screen, focus, and completeness comparison statuses.
- [x] Produce a change record when either comparable dimension changed.
- [x] Preserve affirmative screen-change evidence when focus details are
  incomplete.
- [x] Produce a non-warning incomplete-verification record only when no change
  is affirmatively known.
- [x] Add LuaDoc comments to every new or changed function, class, and
  class-like record.

### Phase 1 tests

- [x] Add `tests/unit/base_screen_focus_guard_spec.lua`.
- [x] Prove identical present identity and focus produce no diagnostic.
- [x] Prove a different screen instance with the same type and focus is a
  screen change.
- [x] Prove `none` compared with `none` is unchanged.
- [x] Prove `none` compared with `present`, in either direction, is a known
  screen change.
- [x] Prove capture failure is unavailable rather than equivalent to `none`.
- [x] Prove a changed focus set on the same screen is a focus change.
- [x] Prove focus ordering and duplicate strings are ignored.
- [x] Prove a known screen change plus unavailable focus produces one change
  warning with incomplete focus details.
- [x] Prove a known focus change plus unavailable screen evidence produces one
  change warning with incomplete screen details.
- [x] Prove entirely unavailable comparison produces an incomplete-
  verification diagnostic instead of a false change warning.
- [x] Prove diagnostic records contain no userdata, mutable source tables, or
  address-bearing labels.
- [x] Prove error strings, focus counts, and focus-string lengths are bounded.

