## Phase 7: Document and close the feature

- [ ] Document example and file-suite pollution warnings in
  `docs/writing-tests.md`.
- [ ] Document the `S0/S2` and `T0/T1` lifecycle boundaries.
- [ ] Explain that one suite is one spec file in one repeat and nested contexts
  do not own suite guards.
- [ ] Explain that suite setup may establish working state but all file
  teardown is expected to restore the inherited `S0`.
- [ ] Explain mounted-component exclusions, warning timing, incomplete
  details, and nonfatal behavior.
- [ ] Document retained warning output and unchanged process-exit semantics in
  `docs/command-line.md`.
- [ ] Add the feature under `Unreleased` in `CHANGELOG.md`.
- [ ] Mark the linked Testing Features item in `docs/project.todo` complete
  only after every implementation and verification gate above is satisfied.
- [ ] Record focused unit, full unit, focused live, full live, event-journal,
  syntax, formatting, process-result, and cleanup evidence below.

